<svg viewBox="0 0 720 440" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Ways to verify factual consistency">
  <!-- two settings -->
  <rect x="40" y="16" width="310" height="78" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="60" y="42" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Local factual consistency</text>
  <text x="60" y="62" font-size="11" fill="var(--ink-soft)">verify against a PROVIDED context — summaries,</text>
  <text x="60" y="78" font-size="11" fill="var(--ink-soft)">support bots vs policy docs, RAG answers</text>

  <rect x="370" y="16" width="310" height="78" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="390" y="42" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Global factual consistency</text>
  <text x="390" y="62" font-size="11" fill="var(--ink-soft)">verify against OPEN knowledge — general chat,</text>
  <text x="390" y="78" font-size="11" fill="var(--ink-soft)">fact-checking · first find facts, then check (harder!)</text>

  <text x="360" y="126" font-size="13.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Verification techniques, lightest to heaviest</text>

  <g font-size="11">
    <rect x="40" y="142" width="640" height="56" rx="9" fill="var(--bg-raised)" stroke="var(--line)" />
    <text x="58" y="165" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">AI judge with a good prompt</text>
    <text x="58" y="184" fill="var(--ink-soft)">“is the summary supported by the source text?” — GPT-4-class judges beat older specialized methods</text>

    <rect x="40" y="208" width="640" height="56" rx="9" fill="var(--bg-raised)" stroke="var(--line)" />
    <text x="58" y="231" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Self-verification (SelfCheckGPT)</text>
    <text x="58" y="250" fill="var(--ink-soft)">sample N fresh responses — if they disagree with the original, it was probably hallucinated · effective but pricey</text>

    <rect x="40" y="274" width="640" height="70" rx="9" fill="var(--bg-raised)" stroke="var(--line)" />
    <text x="58" y="297" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Search-augmented verification (SAFE)</text>
    <text x="58" y="316" fill="var(--ink-soft)">1 · decompose response into atomic statements   2 · rewrite each to be self-contained</text>
    <text x="58" y="332" fill="var(--ink-soft)">3 · issue fact-check queries to a search engine   4 · AI judges each statement vs results</text>

    <rect x="40" y="354" width="640" height="56" rx="9" fill="var(--bg-raised)" stroke="var(--line)" />
    <text x="58" y="377" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Textual entailment as classification</text>
    <text x="58" y="396" fill="var(--ink-soft)">small specialized scorer labels (premise, hypothesis) → entailment / contradiction / neutral — fast and cheap</text>
  </g>

  <text x="360" y="432" font-size="12" font-style="italic" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">Know your hallucination hot spots: niche knowledge, and questions about things that don't exist.</text>
</svg>
